      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was carved out of North Kingstown in 1742, becoming an independent community in the mid‑1700s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exeter%2C_Rhode_Island",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1892, Exeter became the site of the Mercy Brown vampire exhumation, one of America’s most documented cases.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exeter%2C_Rhode_Island",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Tomaquag Museum preserves Narragansett culture, offering a rare glimpse into Rhode Island’s Native American heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
